Task: Add Div 43 capital works item fields (migration 057) (Phase 2, Tier 1)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729

SUMMARY
Adds capital_works_start_date (date) and capital_works_rate_pct
(numeric(5,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 2.5) to public.expenses, plus a partial
index on the start date, plus a backfill.

FILES
- supabase/migrations/057_capital_works_items.sql (new)
- lib/supabase/database.types.ts - both columns added to the expenses
  Row/Insert/Update blocks

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Columns on expenses, not a parallel table. A capital works item IS an
  expense already classified as capital; a separate table would duplicate
  amount, date, supplier and invoice and then need to stay in step through
  reclassification.
- Rate stored per item, defaulted to 2.5%. Eligibility and the applicable
  rate depend on construction date - a QS determination, not the
  product's. Same reasoning as migration 056.
- Backfill prefers renovations.end_date over expenses.expense_date,
  because Div 43 runs from COMPLETION, not from when an invoice was paid.
- The backfill's WHERE clause mirrors resolveTaxClassification in
  lib/tax/classification.ts, including the enum vocabulary difference
  ('capital_improvement' on renovations = 'Capital Works' on expenses).
  Noted in the migration so the two stay in step.

DEFECT CAUGHT DURING VERIFICATION
Initially declared numeric(4,2), which caps at 99.99. That made the
"<= 100" bound unreachable and turned an out-of-range rate into an opaque
"numeric field overflow" rather than a named check violation. Corrected to
numeric(5,2) before commit and re-verified.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED (live, local Supabase)
npm run db:reset -> 57 migrations replayed cleanly from scratch (twice,
once after the precision correction).

Backfill, five seeded expenses across three renovations:
  case  reno_class           override       reno_end     result
  A     capital_improvement  -              2019-11-30   2019-11-30 (end date preferred)
  B     capital_improvement  -              NULL         2024-05-20 (expense date fallback)
  C     repair               Capital Works  2024-02-02   2024-02-02 (override promotes it)
  D     capital_improvement  Repair         2019-11-30   NOT BACKFILLED (override demotes it)
  E     repair               -              2024-02-02   NOT BACKFILLED
UPDATE 3 - exactly the three effective-capital-works rows. Case D is the
one that matters: a manual Repair override on a capital renovation
correctly blocks the backfill.

Idempotency: re-running the backfill -> UPDATE 0.

Rate bounds after the precision fix:
  100.01 -> expenses_capital_works_rate_pct_check (named violation)
  100.00 -> allowed
  4.00   -> allowed (the other rate a QS may determine)
  default on every row -> 2.50

All inside a transaction, rolled back; no local data retained.

npm run build     -> Compiled successfully, no type errors.
CI=true npm test  -> 38 tests passed.

NOTES
